"The patient underwent robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage of pT2. The surgical pathology report documented \"no extraprostatic extension; surgical margins were negative; the seminal vesicles were not invaded; lymphovascular invasion was absent; no lymph nodes were removed.\" Biopsy findings showed a Gleason 0+0 at the first session and Gleason 3+4 at the second session. The absence of documented nodal sampling means that the pNx status does not establish node-negative disease, which widens uncertainty regarding regional disease control. Countervailing findings include negative surgical margins and no seminal vesicle invasion. The prognosis is tempered by the documented negative margins and lack of invasion into the seminal vesicles. Postoperative PSA and its subsequent trajectory are needed to assess biochemical recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory would be crucial in revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 60.33 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 39.21–81.44 months; its coverage has not been validated."
